									<tr>
										<td><!-- InstanceBeginEditable name="Text" -->
<p class="callout_box"><strong>Visit individual websites below to see program details for 18 Workshops</strong></p>
										<h3>ABOUT IPDPS WORKSHOPS</h3>
										
										<p>Held on two consecutive days of the five-day conference, IPDPS workshops provide an extended forum that allows the IPDPS community an opportunity to fully explore special topics and to present work that is more preliminary and cutting-edge or that has more practical content than the more mature research presented in the main symposium. Each workshop has its own requirements and submission schedule. Workshop paper submission dates typically fall after the notification date for the main symposium papers. Proceedings of the workshops are distributed at the conference and are submitted for inclusion in the IEEE Xplore Digital Library after the conference.</p>
										<p>IPDPS 2026 and all associated events, including workshops, are scheduled to be held in person between the dates of May 25-29, 2026, in New Orleans, USA. For IPDPS 2026, we are holding all workshops &amp; tutorials during the first two days of the conference, i.e., on May 25th and May 26th, 2026. The schedule and location of all events will be available in the <a href="https://ssl.linklings.net/conferences/ipdps/ipdps2026_program/views/at_a_glance.html">online conference program here</a>.</p>
									
<h3>WORKSHOPS CO-CHAIRS</h3>
										<p>Suren Byna (The Ohio State University, USA)<br>
											Giulia Guidi (Cornell University, USA)<br>
											Francieli Boito (University of Bordeaux, France)<br>
	<a href="mailto:workshops@ipdps.org"><strong>workshops@ipdps.org</strong></a></p>
										
										<h3>VISIT WORKSHOP WEBSITES BELOW TO SEE PLANNED PROGRAM</h3>
										<p><em>Note that all workshops have their own Web sites and may make changes in their program and speakers until several weeks before the conference.</em></p>
										<h3>IPDPS 2026 WORKSHOPS – To be held Monday 25 May</h3>
